  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Making Aquaculture Cooperatives in MRD Inclusive and Bankable (MACIB Mekong Project)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mekong River Delta (MDR), a vital agricultural region facing climate change threats, particularly benefits from the project, which aligns with Vietnamese and Dutch government priorities. The aquaculture sector in the region, significant for its economic contribution, faces challenges like fragmented production and environmental pressures.The initiative seeks to make aquaculture cooperatives in the Mekong River Delta, Vietnam, self-sufficient and financially viable, enabling them to access financing and fostering inclusivity. It focuses on professionalising cooperatives, providing support for sustainable aquaculture practices, and empowering underrepresented groups like women and youth. Advocacy efforts aim to advance cooperative interests, while collaboration within the sector is promoted to strengthen partnerships.Agriterra&apos;s three-year proposal targets governance, business development, financial management, and productivity improvement in aquaculture cooperatives to enhance economic development and attract private sector investment, ultimately aiming for sustainability and resilience in the industry.</narrative>
  </description>
